  ],
  "description": "Positive-ground 3 V FZ-1 as traced by Andy Rothstein from Vinnie Zummo’s 1962 unit, with three 2N270 PNPs, 1.5 kΩ Q2 collector load, 470 kΩ Q2 bias resistor and 3.3 nF output coupling. Gert Willmann’s room-temperature fit from Greg Whitehead’s US3213181 study supplies the 2N270 device values. Three explicit junctions represent its collector-base leakage (ISC 8.35 µA, NC 1.7). Temperature variation, charge storage and high-current rolloff are omitted. The specimen’s 500 kΩ Volume and 50 kΩ Attack pots use assumed linear travel.",
  "groundNode": "0",
  "inputNode": "in",
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "Attack",
      "Volume"
    ]
  },
  "name": "Maestro FZ-1 Fuzz-Tone 1962",
  "outputNode": "out",
  "version": 3,
